        "id": 63519,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-05-22T22:58:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>You may not like the way I rationalize the occurences of that happen in the game. My whole&nbsp;point is that things can be interpreted anyway the player wishes to. So a hero attacking another hero at the players whim could be any number of things, maybe the hero is hitting the other just because they want to or&nbsp;maybe it is because the hero&nbsp;wants the other to stay back out of harms way so the attacking hero can cut-loose on the villain. Either way they are both fine ways of thinking about it. There are still plenty of other ways to think about how it works aswell. So it can still be played very thematically if&nbsp;one think outside of dealing damage as the heroes actually attacking things. Is Visionary really that powerful to&nbsp;demoralize a ship?</p>",
